","_margin":{"unit":"px","top":"14","right":"0","bottom":"0","left":"0","isLinked":false}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"3051622","elType":"widget","settings":{"tabs":[{"tab_title":"How much does it cost to develop an AI agent in 2025?","tab_content":"<p>The cost to develop an AI agent in 2025 typically ranges from $5,000 to $100,000+, depending on the complexity, type of agent, features, and integrations you need.</p><p>For example, a basic chatbot or FAQ bot might cost around $5,000–$15,000, while an advanced AI Sales Agent or Code Agent powered by GPT models can range from $40,000 upwards.</p><p>At ReapMind, we customize pricing based on your business goals, not just your tech stack.</p>","_id":"afe7f8c"},{"tab_title":"What factors influence the cost of AI agent development?","tab_content":"<p>Several factors affect AI agent development pricing, including:</p><ul><li>The type of agent (Sales, HR, Support, Code, or Marketing)</li><li>The level of intelligence (rule-based vs. machine learning vs. generative AI)'</li><li>The amount and quality of data used for AI model training</li><li>Integration needs with your CRM, ERP, or third-party tools</li><li>Post-launch maintenance and support requirements</li></ul><p>Each of these directly impacts the overall AI agent project budget.</p>","_id":"1956e90"},{"tab_title":"How long does it take to build an AI agent?","tab_content":"<p>On average, it takes 4 to 12 weeks to build and deploy a functional AI agent.</p><ul><li>Simple bots can be ready in under a month.</li><li>Smarter agents that include custom workflows, NLP, and self-learning capabilities can take 3–6 months.<br />ReapMind follows an agile approach — so you get quick MVPs and can scale your AI agent feature by feature.</li></ul>","_id":"1ea7759"},{"tab_title":"What are the main types of AI agents businesses are using today?","tab_content":"<p>The most popular categories of AI agents include:</p><ul><li><strong>Sales Agents:</strong> Automate lead 